sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Authenticated User
    participant Workstation as RecordsWorkstation UI
    participant BGRecorder as BackgroundRecorder
    participant Store as Workspace Store
    participant DG as Deepgram WebSocket API
    participant BFF as Next.js BFF Server<br/>(/api/records)
    participant DB as Neon PostgreSQL
    participant S3 as S3 Object Storage<br/>(MinIO / AWS S3)

    %% Recording & Live Transcription
    User->>Workstation: Click "Record"
    activate Workstation
    Workstation->>Store: setIsRecording(true)
    activate Store
    Store-->>BGRecorder: state change event
    deactivate Store
    activate BGRecorder
    BGRecorder->>BGRecorder: Initialize navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia()
    BGRecorder->>DG: Open WebSocket connection (Primary: Vietnamese)
    activate DG
    BGRecorder->>BGRecorder: Start MediaRecorder audio capture
    BGRecorder-->>Workstation: Render waveform visualizer at 60fps
    deactivate Workstation

    loop Speak into Mic
        BGRecorder->>DG: Stream raw audio packets
        DG-->>BGRecorder: Stream live transcription chunks
        BGRecorder->>Store: setLiveTranscript(transcript)
        activate Store
        Store-->>Workstation: Render text scrolling in real-time
        deactivate Store
    end

    User->>Workstation: Click "Stop"
    activate Workstation
    Workstation->>Store: setIsRecording(false)
    activate Store
    Store-->>BGRecorder: state change event
    deactivate Store
    BGRecorder->>BGRecorder: Stop MediaRecorder & capture final Blob
    BGRecorder->>DG: Close WebSocket
    deactivate DG
    BGRecorder->>BGRecorder: Store Audio Blob in Local Cache (CaptureQueue)
    BGRecorder-->>Workstation: Show player timeline controls
    deactivate BGRecorder
    deactivate Workstation

    %% Persisting Recording Metadata and Audio File
    User->>Workstation: Fill Title & click "Save"
    activate Workstation
    Workstation->>BFF: POST /api/records { title, transcript, durationSec }
    activate BFF
    BFF->>DB: Insert record metadata via Prisma
    activate DB
    DB-->>BFF: recordCreated (with ID)
    deactivate DB
    BFF-->>Workstation: HTTP 200 OK (record object with ID)
    deactivate BFF

    Workstation->>Workstation: Retrieve Audio Blob from local cache
    Workstation->>BFF: POST /api/records/upload (FormData: audio, recordingId)
    activate BFF
    BFF->>S3: Upload raw WebM file to bucket (AWS SDK)
    activate S3
    S3-->>BFF: File saved & return S3 URL
    deactivate S3
    BFF->>DB: Update record with S3 Audio URL
    activate DB
    DB-->>BFF: recordUpdated
    deactivate DB
    BFF-->>Workstation: HTTP 200 OK (audioUploaded)
    deactivate BFF

    Workstation->>Store: resetRecordingState() & refreshRecordings()
    activate Store
    Store->>BFF: GET /api/records
    activate BFF
    BFF->>DB: Query all user records
    activate DB
    DB-->>BFF: recordsList
    deactivate DB
    BFF-->>Store: HTTP 200 OK (recordings array)
    deactivate BFF
    Store-->>Workstation: Re-render records catalog list
    deactivate Store
    Workstation-->>User: Show "Save successful" toast notification
    deactivate Workstation
